// automations.memql -- harness namespace (#586, epic #590).
//
// Memory consolidation: the scheduled pass that distills raw EPISODIC
// memory (plans / steps / observations from #582) into durable
// SEMANTIC memory (v1:harness:semanticMemory). This is what makes the
// harness feel cognitive rather than merely durable -- analogous to
// memory consolidation during sleep.
//
// The whole point is that this is a scheduled DSL automation that reads
// and writes the SAME graph. Provenance is the killer feature: every
// distilled belief (semanticMemory.sourceEpisodes) traces back to the
// episodic nodes that formed it, so a belief is always auditable. No
// external job system, no separate belief store, no separate watermark
// file -- it is all MemoryNodes.
//
//   scheduled tick
//     -> read recent episodic nodes since the per-owner watermark
//     -> group by similarity
//     -> LLM distill: extract stable facts / preferences / outcomes
//     -> dedup via similarTo against existing semanticMemory rows
//          match    -> reinforce (bump confidence, reset decay clock,
//                      merge provenance) -- NO duplicate row
//          no match -> write a new semanticMemory with sourceEpisodes
//     -> decay + prune stale, unreinforced beliefs
//     -> advance the per-owner watermark (incremental: next run reads
//        only newer episodes, so cost is bounded as history grows)
//
// SCHEDULE: daily 02:45 UTC. Offset 5 minutes past the safety crons
// (02:35 / 02:40) and 15 past the knowledge / platform crons (02:30)
// so the nightly maintenance crons don't contend on the same DB
// window. Daily cadence matches the "consolidation during sleep"
// framing -- beliefs are durable, so distilling once a day is plenty;
// the watermark guarantees nothing is missed between runs.

use harness.logic.{ logicConsolidateMemory }

@enabled
@trigger(schedule="0 45 2 * * *")
@description("Daily 02:45 UTC memory consolidation (#586). Per owner: reads episodic nodes (plans / steps / observations) created since that owner's v1:harness:consolidationCursor watermark, groups them by similarity, LLM-distills stable facts / preferences / outcomes, dedups each candidate via similarTo against existing v1:harness:semanticMemory rows (reinforce on match -- bump confidence + reset the decay clock + merge provenance, no duplicate; write a new belief with sourceEpisodes provenance on no match), decays + prunes stale unreinforced beliefs, then advances the watermark so the next run is incremental (cost bounded by the new-episode delta, not total history). Schedule offset past the other nightly crons to avoid DB-window contention.")
automation consolidateMemory {
  step run {
    logic consolidateMemory { event: event }
  }
}
